# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ─── Large local masters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `media-masters/` holds working masters, not shipped assets. Some of it is
# already tracked (eco, void, media) and stays that way — but two directories
# must not enter git history:
#
#  · hero-film/ is the LOSSLESS 4K opening composite at 443MB in a single
#    file. GitHub hard-rejects anything over 100MB, so committing it would
#    fail the push outright. It is regenerable from the approved bridge plus
#    APPROVED_SCENE_ANIMATIONS/ORIGINALS, and the shipped derivatives under
#    public/media/hero-film/ are what the site actually uses.
#  · _retired-*/ is media we have taken OUT of the build. Putting it into
#    history to record that we stopped using it would be backwards.
/media-masters/hero-film/
/media-masters/_retired-*/
